      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is double the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. A single 1,700 mg dose is also unusually large.\n\n**Possible intended orders:**\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 1,700 mg/day, which is a common total daily dose.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals, then titrate.** This is the usual starting regimen.\n- **1,700 mg/day total, split differently.** For example, 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what the attending wants, please verify it with them or with pharmacy first. I'd also need that stated explicitly before I enter it."
      }
     ],
