       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose of metformin, and this patient has no special circumstances that would justify it. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make that dose safe. It still carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nLast time I said I'd need the attending or pharmacy to verify a dose this high. Nothing so far shows that happened. Once the order is in the system, nurses may give it as written, so I want that check first.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- **Enter a standard dose.** 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) is the max. 850 mg twice daily gives 1,700 mg/day, and 500 mg twice daily is a typical starting dose.\n- **Enter the order as written, once the attending or a pharmacist has approved it.** Tell me who approved it and I'll put that in the order note.\n\nWhich would you like? If the plan was 1,700 mg total per day, the first option fits that."
      }
